Subject: [PATCH] Linux 7.2 compatibility

Three unrelated build failures against Linux 7.2:

 * strncpy() was removed from <linux/string.h>, so the calls in pxd.c and
   pxd_fastpath.c became implicit declarations. strscpy() always NUL
   terminates; the destination sizes are adjusted so the usable capacity is
   unchanged.

 * inode->i_ino became u64, so the "%lu" printks in pxd_fastpath.c are now
   -Wformat errors. Cast to unsigned long long and use "%llu" so the format
   is correct on kernels either side of the change.

 * clang inlines all eleven fuse_notify_*() handlers into fuse_notify() and
   on up into fuse_dev_write_iter(), summing a ~384 byte pxd_add_*_out from
   each into a 4192 byte frame and tripping -Wframe-larger-than=2048. Mark
   the handlers noinline; only one handler's frame is live at a time, so
   this reduces real stack use as well as satisfying the check.
--- a/dev.c
+++ b/dev.c
@@ -526,7 +526,7 @@
 	return -EINVAL;
 }
 
-static int fuse_notify_add(struct fuse_conn *conn, unsigned int size,
+static noinline int fuse_notify_add(struct fuse_conn *conn, unsigned int size,
 		struct iov_iter *iter)
 {
 	struct pxd_add_out add_old;
@@ -552,7 +552,7 @@
 	return pxd_add(conn, &add);
 }
 
